\s1 The Temple Cleansed
\p \v 4 \w Now before|strong="H6440"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w*, \w Eliashib|strong="H475"\w* \w the priest|strong="H3548"\w*, \w a relative|strong="H7138"\w* \w of Tobiah|strong="H2900"\w*, \w had been put in charge of|strong="H5414"\w* \w the storerooms|strong="H3957"\w* \w of the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of our God|strong="H430"\w* \v 5 \w and had prepared|strong="H6213"\w* for [Tobiah] \w a large|strong="H1419"\w* \w room|strong="H3957"\w* \w where|strong="H8033"\w* \w . . .|strong="H1961"\w* \w they had previously|strong="H6440"\w* \w stored|strong="H5414"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w the grain offerings|strong="H4503"\w*, \w the frankincense|strong="H3828"\w*, \w the [temple] articles|strong="H3627"\w*, \w and the tithes|strong="H4643"\w* \w of grain|strong="H1715"\w*, \w new wine|strong="H8492"\w*, \w and oil|strong="H3323"\w* \w prescribed|strong="H4687"\w* \w for the Levites|strong="H3881"\w*, \w singers|strong="H7891"\w*, \w and gatekeepers|strong="H7778"\w*, \w along with the contributions|strong="H8641"\w* \w for the priests|strong="H3548"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w While all|strong="H3605"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w was happening|strong="H1961"\w*, \w I was not|strong="H3808"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w I had returned|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Artaxerxes|strong="H783"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*\f + \fr 13:6 \ft Artaxerxes king of Persia is identified here as the king of Babylon because Persia had conquered the Babylonian Empire.\f* \w in the thirty-second|strong="H7970"\w* \w . . .|strong="H8147"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of his reign|strong="H4428"\w*. \w Some time later|strong="H7093"\w* \w . . .|strong="H3117"\w* \w I obtained leave|strong="H7592"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \v 7 \w to return|strong="H935"\w* \w to Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*. \w Then I discovered|strong="H995"\w* \w the evil|strong="H7451"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Eliashib|strong="H475"\w* \w had done|strong="H6213"\w* \w on behalf of Tobiah|strong="H2900"\w* \w by providing|strong="H6213"\w* him \w a room|strong="H5393"\w* \w in the courts|strong="H2691"\w* \w of the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of God|strong="H430"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w And I was greatly|strong="H3966"\w* \w displeased|strong="H7489"\w* \w and threw|strong="H7993"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w of Tobiah’s|strong="H2900"\w* \w household|strong="H1004"\w* \w goods|strong="H3627"\w* \w out|strong="H2351"\w* \w of|strong="H4480"\w* \w the room|strong="H3957"\w*. \v 9 \w Then I ordered|strong="H559"\w* \w that the rooms|strong="H3957"\w* \w be purified|strong="H2891"\w*, \w and I had the articles|strong="H3627"\w* \w of the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of God|strong="H430"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w restored|strong="H7725"\w* \w to them|strong="H8033"\w*, \w along with the grain offerings|strong="H4503"\w* \w and frankincense|strong="H3828"\w*.
\s1 Tithes Restored
\r (\ref Leviticus 27:30–34|LEV 27:30-34\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 14:22–29|DEU 14:22-29\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 26:1–15|DEU 26:1-15\ref*)
\p \v 10 \w I also learned|strong="H3045"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w because the portions|strong="H4521"\w* \w for the Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w had not|strong="H3808"\w* \w been given to them|strong="H5414"\w*, \w all|strong="H376"\w* \w the Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w and singers|strong="H7891"\w* \w responsible for performing|strong="H6213"\w* \w the service|strong="H4399"\w* \w had gone back|strong="H1272"\w* \w to their own fields|strong="H7704"\w*. \v 11 \w So I rebuked|strong="H7378"\w*\w . . .|strong="H854"\w* \w the officials|strong="H5461"\w* \w and asked|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Why|strong="H4069"\w* \w has the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of God|strong="H430"\w* \w been neglected|strong="H5800"\w*?”
\p \w Then I gathered the Levites and singers together|strong="H6908"\w* \w and stationed them|strong="H5975"\w* \w at|strong="H5921"\w* \w their posts|strong="H5977"\w*, \v 12 \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w brought|strong="H935"\w* \w a tenth|strong="H4643"\w* \w of the grain|strong="H1715"\w*, \w new wine|strong="H8492"\w*, \w and oil|strong="H3323"\w* \w into the storerooms|strong="H214"\w*. \v 13 \w I appointed as treasurers|strong="H686"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w the storerooms|strong="H214"\w* \w Shelemiah|strong="H8018"\w* \w the priest|strong="H3548"\w*, \w Zadok|strong="H6659"\w* \w the scribe|strong="H5608"\w*, \w and Pedaiah|strong="H6305"\w* \w of|strong="H4480"\w* \w the Levites|strong="H3881"\w*, \w with Hanan|strong="H2605"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zaccur|strong="H2139"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Mattaniah|strong="H4983"\w*, \w to assist|strong="H5921"\w* \w them|strong="H3027"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w they were considered|strong="H2803"\w* \w trustworthy|strong="H539"\w*. \w They were responsible for|strong="H5921"\w* \w distributing the supplies|strong="H2505"\w* \w to their fellow [Levites]|strong="H251"\w*.
\p \v 14 \w Remember|strong="H2142"\w* me \w for|strong="H5921"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w*, \w O my God|strong="H430"\w*, \w and do not|strong="H408"\w* \w blot out|strong="H4229"\w* \w my deeds of loving devotion|strong="H2617"\w* \w -|strong="H834"\w* \w -|strong="H6213"\w* \w for the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of my God|strong="H430"\w* \w and for its services|strong="H4929"\w*.
\s1 The Sabbath Restored
\r (\ref Jeremiah 17:19–27|JER 17:19-27\ref*)
\p \v 15 \w In those|strong="H1992"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w I saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w people in Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w treading|strong="H1869"\w* \w winepresses|strong="H1660"\w* \w on the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w and bringing in|strong="H935"\w* \w grain|strong="H6194"\w* \w and loading it|strong="H6006"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w donkeys|strong="H2543"\w*, \w along with|strong="H637"\w* \w wine|strong="H3196"\w*, \w grapes|strong="H6025"\w*, \w and figs|strong="H8384"\w*. \w All kinds|strong="H3605"\w* \w of goods|strong="H4853"\w* \w were being brought|strong="H935"\w* \w into Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w on the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*. \w So I warned them|strong="H5749"\w* \w against selling|strong="H4376"\w* \w food|strong="H6718"\w* \w on that day|strong="H3117"\w*. \v 16 \w Additionally, [men of] Tyre|strong="H6876"\w* \w who lived|strong="H3427"\w* there \w were importing|strong="H935"\w* \w fish|strong="H1709"\w* \w and all kinds|strong="H3605"\w* \w of merchandise|strong="H4377"\w* \w and selling them|strong="H4376"\w* \w on the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w to the people|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*.
\p \v 17 \w Then I rebuked|strong="H7378"\w* \w . . .|strong="H854"\w* \w the nobles|strong="H2715"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and asked|strong="H559"\w*, “\w What|strong="H4100"\w* \w . . .|strong="H1697"\w* \w is this|strong="H2088"\w* \w -|strong="H834"\w* \w evil|strong="H7451"\w* \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w are doing|strong="H6213"\w*— \w profaning|strong="H2490"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*? \v 18 \w Did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w your forefathers|strong="H1"\w* \w do|strong="H6213"\w* \w the same things|strong="H3541"\w*, \w so that our God|strong="H430"\w* \w brought|strong="H935"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w disaster|strong="H7451"\w* \w on us|strong="H5921"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w and on|strong="H5921"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*? \w And now|strong="H859"\w* \w you are rekindling|strong="H3254"\w* \w His wrath|strong="H2740"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w by profaning|strong="H2490"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w*!”
\p \v 19 \w -|strong="H1961"\w* \w When|strong="H834"\w* \w the evening shadows|strong="H6751"\w* \w began to fall on the gates|strong="H8179"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*, \w just before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w*, \w I ordered|strong="H559"\w* \w that the gates|strong="H1817"\w* \w . . .|strong="H559"\w* \w -|strong="H834"\w* \w be shut|strong="H5462"\w* \w and not|strong="H3808"\w* \w opened|strong="H6605"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w after|strong="H310"\w* \w the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w*. \w I posted|strong="H5975"\w* \w some of my servants|strong="H5288"\w* \w at|strong="H5921"\w* \w the gates|strong="H8179"\w* \w so that no|strong="H3808"\w* \w load|strong="H4853"\w* \w could enter|strong="H935"\w* \w on the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.
\p \v 20 \w Once|strong="H6471"\w* \w or twice|strong="H8147"\w*, \w the merchants|strong="H7402"\w* \w and those who sell|strong="H4376"\w* \w all kinds|strong="H3605"\w* \w of goods|strong="H4465"\w* \w camped|strong="H3885"\w* \w outside|strong="H2351"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*, \v 21 \w but I warned|strong="H5749"\w* them \w -|strong="H559"\w* \w -|strong="H413"\w*, “\w Why|strong="H4069"\w* \w are you|strong="H859"\w* \w camping|strong="H3885"\w* \w in front of|strong="H5048"\w* \w the wall|strong="H2346"\w*? \w If|strong="H518"\w* \w you do it again|strong="H8138"\w*, \w I will lay|strong="H7971"\w* \w hands|strong="H3027"\w* on you.” \w From|strong="H4480"\w* \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w time on|strong="H6256"\w*, \w they did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w return|strong="H935"\w* \w on the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w*. \v 22 \w Then I instructed|strong="H559"\w* \w the Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w -|strong="H834"\w* \w -|strong="H1961"\w* \w to purify themselves|strong="H2891"\w* \w . . .|strong="H935"\w* \w and guard|strong="H8104"\w* \w the gates|strong="H8179"\w* \w in order to keep the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w holy|strong="H6942"\w*. \w -|strong="H853"\w*
\p \w Remember|strong="H2142"\w* me \w for this|strong="H2063"\w* \w as well|strong="H1571"\w*, \w O my God|strong="H430"\w*, \w and {show} me|strong="H5921"\w* \w mercy|strong="H2347"\w* \w according to Your abundant|strong="H7230"\w* \w loving devotion|strong="H2617"\w*.
\s1 Intermarriage Forbidden
\r (\ref Ezra 9:1–4|EZR 9:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 23 \w In those|strong="H1992"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w I also|strong="H1571"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w Jews|strong="H3064"\w* \w who had married|strong="H3427"\w* \w women|strong="H802"\w* \w from Ashdod|strong="H796"\w*, \w Ammon|strong="H5984"\w*, \w and Moab|strong="H4125"\w*. \v 24 \w Half|strong="H2677"\w* \w of their children|strong="H1121"\w* \w spoke|strong="H1696"\w* \w the language of Ashdod|strong="H797"\w* \w or of|strong="H3956"\w* \w the other peoples|strong="H5971"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H5971"\w* \w but could|strong="H5234"\w* \w not|strong="H369"\w* \w speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w the language of Judah|strong="H3066"\w*. \v 25 \w I rebuked them|strong="H7378"\w* \w . . .|strong="H5973"\w* \w and called down curses on them|strong="H7043"\w*. \w I beat|strong="H5221"\w* some of \w these men|strong="H582"\w* \w and pulled out their hair|strong="H4803"\w*.
\p \w Then I made them take an oath|strong="H7650"\w* \w before God [and said]|strong="H430"\w*, “\w You must not|strong="H518"\w* \w give your daughters|strong="H1323"\w* \w in marriage|strong="H5414"\w* \w to their sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H518"\w* \w or take|strong="H5375"\w* \w their daughters|strong="H1323"\w* \w as wives for your sons|strong="H1121"\w* or for yourselves! \v 26 \w Did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Solomon|strong="H8010"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w sin|strong="H2398"\w* \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w matters like this|strong="H428"\w*? \w There was|strong="H1961"\w* \w not|strong="H3808"\w* \w a king|strong="H4428"\w* \w like him|strong="H3644"\w* \w among many|strong="H7227"\w* \w nations|strong="H1471"\w*, \w and he was|strong="H1961"\w* \w loved|strong="H157"\w* \w by his God|strong="H430"\w*, \w [who]|strong="H430"\w* \w made him|strong="H5414"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*— \w yet|strong="H1571"\w* \w foreign|strong="H5237"\w* \w women|strong="H802"\w* \w vvv|strong="H853"\w* \w drew him into sin|strong="H2398"\w*. \v 27 vvv \w Must we now hear|strong="H8085"\w* \w that you too are doing|strong="H6213"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w terrible|strong="H1419"\w* \w evil|strong="H7451"\w* \w and acting unfaithfully|strong="H4603"\w* \w against our God|strong="H430"\w* \w by marrying|strong="H3427"\w* \w foreign|strong="H5237"\w* \w women|strong="H802"\w*?”
\p \v 28 \w Even one of the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Jehoiada|strong="H3111"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Eliashib|strong="H475"\w* \w the high|strong="H1419"\w* \w priest|strong="H3548"\w* \w had become a son-in-law|strong="H2860"\w* \w to Sanballat|strong="H5571"\w* \w the Horonite|strong="H2772"\w*. \w Therefore I drove him away|strong="H1272"\w* \w from me|strong="H5921"\w*.
\p \v 29 \w Remember|strong="H2142"\w* them, \w O my God|strong="H430"\w*, \w because|strong="H5921"\w* \w they have defiled|strong="H1352"\w* \w the priesthood|strong="H3550"\w* \w and the covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w of the priesthood|strong="H3550"\w* \w and of the Levites|strong="H3881"\w*.
\p \v 30 \w Thus I purified [the priests and Levites]|strong="H2891"\w* \w from everything|strong="H3605"\w* \w foreign|strong="H5236"\w*, \w and I assigned|strong="H5975"\w* \w specific|strong="H4399"\w* \w duties|strong="H4931"\w* \w to each|strong="H376"\w* \w of the priests|strong="H3548"\w* \w and Levites|strong="H3881"\w*. \v 31 \w I also arranged for contributions|strong="H7133"\w* \w of wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w at the appointed|strong="H2163"\w* \w times|strong="H6256"\w*, \w and for the firstfruits|strong="H1061"\w*.
\p \w Remember|strong="H2142"\w* me, \w O my God|strong="H430"\w*, \w with favor|strong="H2896"\w*.
